    "description": "The operational heart of an incident-response app: an incident lifecycle (new \u2192 acknowledged \u2192 responding \u2192 resolved) that can be triggered by external events, workflows, or created manually. Kanban triage board, acknowledge/resolve actions, and SLA escalation via the core escalate-unless timer \u2014 acknowledge in time and the escalation is cancelled, miss it and severity bumps and the on-call is paged. Vendor-neutral: an incident doesn't care whether it came from a detection platform, a form, or a person.",
